{"title":"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following numbers is a perfect square?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/3/be304be7ca92a9b1859e34a10b27a8f83f379222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 98! \\cdot 99! \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 98! \\cdot 100! \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 99! \\cdot 100! \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 99! \\cdot 101! \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 100! \\cdot 101!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"638\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/0/ff06c43a1fea23ceef30b8f477e0df554af5e550.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n! = n\\cdot (n-1)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />, we can write:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c6a7be94573285f6b307d0d2c6ed71c6aab7771.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align} A&amp;=98! \\cdot (99\\cdot 98!) = 99 \\cdot (98!)^2 = 11\\cdot3^2\\cdot(98!)^2 \\\\ B&amp;=100 \\cdot 99 \\cdot (98!)^2 = 11\\cdot10^2\\cdot3^2\\cdot( 98!)^2 \\\\ C&amp;=100\\cdot (99!)^2 = 10^2\\cdot (99!)^2\\\\ D&amp;=101\\cdot 100\\cdot (99!)^2 = 101 \\cdot 10^2 \\cdot (99!)^2\\\\ E&amp; =101\\cdot (100!)^2 \\end{align}\" width=\"425\" height=\"130\" />\n</p><p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/d/3cdcea95e05ffe882f15dc7800925d0720627c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(C) \\ } 99! \\cdot 100!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"113\" height=\"29\" /> is a square, and because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> are primes, none of the other four choices are squares.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd629034145b95656ef371c2f5abe03bd3df687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99! \\cdot 99!$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is a perfect square (obviously). Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8573e266358e2e60508d81fba091e34120f5c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 = 10^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea94e4bcc1fe32d3c88103e712c1e5fd0b38b686.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(99!)^2 \\cdot 10^2 = 99! \\cdot 100!\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"19\" /> \nis a perfect square, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/d/3cdcea95e05ffe882f15dc7800925d0720627c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(C) \\ } 99! \\cdot 100!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"113\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B\">2004 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"cent